<title>GERMANY: Waigel says OECD report backs Bonn reform efforts.</title>
<headline>Waigel says OECD report backs Bonn reform efforts.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Thursday that the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development's (OECD) report on Germany leant support to the government's fiscal reforms ahead of Europe's single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;The OECD Economic Outlook reiterates the need for further fiscal consolidation and thereby supports the path that the federal government has embarked upon,&quot; Waigel said in a statement issued in Bonn.</p>
<p>He added that the OECD shared Bonn's view that Germany's economic recovery would continue next year, but added that &quot;Structural reforms must be undertaken on a broad front to ensure lasting improvements in economic performance.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
